<title>SWEDEN: Marieberg paid 555 mln skr for TV4 stake.</title>
<headline>Marieberg paid 555 mln skr for TV4 stake.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish media company Tidnings AB Marieberg said on Tuesday it paid around 555 million crowns for Swedish insurance company SPP's stake in TV4 as well as TV4 shares from Foreningsbanken's share portfolio.  </p>
<p>Marieberg said in a statement it had acquired 193,184 A series shares and 2,753,220 B series shares from Swedish insurance company SPP. It also said it had acquired 400,000 A series shares of TV4 from Foreningsbanken.</p>
<p>The acquisition was equal to 16.7 percent of the capital in TV4 and, after conversion of the B shares to A shares, the same share of voting rights, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;Together the purchasing price is about 555 million crowns,&quot; Marieberg said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1003</p>
